  {
   "id": "plebox",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 700,
   "y": -252,
   "width": 260,
   "height": 1120,
   "text": "**per-layer input** slice *i* [T, 256] → **layer i**  \n\nInside each layer, after the FFN: gate 2560→256, GELU, × slice, project 256→2560, RMSNorm, + residual (1.3M per layer).  \n\nSo every layer sees its own learned 256-number code for the current token — extra capacity that costs a table lookup, not a matmul.",
   "color": "#a3e635"
  },
  {
   "id": "kvown",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -440,
   "y": -302,
   "width": 270,
   "height": 552,
   "text": "**L0–23 compute K/V**    \nKV cache per token: sliding 1,024 values (2 × 2 × 256), full 2,048 (2 × 2 × 512).  \n\nL22 (last sliding) and L23 (last full) keep their K/V for the shared layers below.",
   "color": "#94a3b8"
  },
  {
   "id": "kvsh",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -440,
   "y": 316,
   "width": 270,
   "height": 552,
   "text": "**L24–41: KV sharing** — 18 layers have no k_proj / v_proj in use and no cache of their own. Sliding layers attend over L22's K/V, full layers (L29, L35, L41) over L23's.  \n\nCache shrinks from 42 to 24 layers' worth. The checkpoint still stores their K/V weights (55.1M); transformers drops them on load.",
   "color": "#f59e0b"
  },
  {
   "id": "img17",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -1050,
   "y": -960,
   "width": 300,
   "height": 56,
   "text": "**image / video frame** pixels",
   "color": "#64748b"
  },
  {
   "id": "vp18",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -931,
   "y": -864,
   "width": 61,
   "height": 9,
   "text": "",
   "color": "#64748b"
  },
  {
   "id": "note-lbl19",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -1510,
   "y": -874,
   "width": 440,
   "height": 34,
   "text": "`patches [P, 768]  (16×16×3)`"
  },
  {
   "id": "vpe20",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -1050,
   "y": -810,
   "width": 300,
   "height": 72,
   "text": "**patch embed** 768 → 768  \n+ learned x/y position tables  \n16.3M",
   "color": "#a78bfa"
  },
  {
   "id": "v021",
